.040.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.040</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC3319071</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">22424230</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Koutsodendris N, Nelson MR, Rao A, and Huang Y (2022). Apolipoprotein E and Alzheimer&#x2019;s Disease: Findings, Hypotheses, and Potential Mechanisms. Annu. Rev. Pathol. Mech. Dis 17, 73&#x2013;99. 10.1146/annurev-pathmechdis-030421-112756.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1146/annurev-pathmechdis-030421-112756</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">34460318</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Long JM, and Holtzman DM (2019). Alzheimer Disease: An Update on Pathobiology and Treatment Strategies. Cell 179, 312&#x2013;339. 10.1016/j.cell.2019.09.001.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.cell.2019.09.001</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6778042</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">31564456</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Najm R, Jones EA, and Huang Y (2019). Apolipoprotein E4, inhibitory network dysfunction, and Alzheimer&#x2019;s disease. Mol. Neurodegener 14, 24. 10.1186/s13024-019-0324-6.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1186/s13024-019-0324-6</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6558779</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">31186040</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Yamazaki Y, Zhao N, Caulfield TR, Liu C-C, and Bu G (2019). Apolipoprotein E and Alzheimer disease: pathobiology and targeting strategies. Nat. Rev. Neurol 15, 501&#x2013;518. 10.1038/s41582-019-0228-7.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/s41582-019-0228-7</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC7055192</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">31367008</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Farrer LA, Cupples LA, Haines JL, Hyman B, Kukull WA, Mayeux R, Myers RH, Pericak-Vance MA, Risch N, and 